// Regression: a sync fn whose body is a single `await spawn f()`
// expression (no `return` keyword -- "implicit return" form)
// crashed the compiler with "missing terminator in basic block
// 'await.ok'".  Pre-fix the ExprStmt-body handler emitted the
// `ret` on the original `block` argument, but await splits
// control flow so `cg.curBlock` had moved on to the `await.ok`
// success-path block.  The original entry block was already
// terminated by the conditional branch into await.ok/await.panic,
// so emitTerminator's `b.Term != nil` early-return fired and NO
// terminator landed anywhere.  The dangling `await.ok` block
// panicked during IR serialization in mod.String().
//
// Fix: prefer cg.curBlock (the block where the awaited result is
// live) over the stale `block` arg for the terminator.

fn{#async} dbl(n i64) i64 = return n + n

fn main() i64 = await spawn dbl(5)
